      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel that way when the effort of self-presentation becomes too much. That feeling of an empty, un-rechargeable battery points to deep, persistent emotional exhaustion. The pressure to \"perform\" life for others is immense, and it's okay to be tired of the in-between. A therapist or mental health professional can help you explore ways to stop trying to \"perform\" and start trying to *be* in a way that feels real to you.",
      "source": "target",
